Z||000072||FieroHarry||06-16-2001||08:30 AM||||As a younger and dumber fool, I survived a nasty crash because I was drunk and flopping around in the car like a fish out of water.<BR>Since being in the Navy for the last 19+ years I have seen many wrecks where seatbelts have saved many a persons life.<BR>I wear them............<BR>I make every body who rides with me wear them.<BR>They put them there for a reason, not to just look nice!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||1
Z||000073||fierohoho||06-16-2001||08:44 AM||||Physics. <P>The kinetic energy on a human body in a 30mph crash into a stationary object, in this case lets say a brick wall, is the same as a fall from a height of 30 feet to the ground. <P>If I drop you face first 30' can you land without injury?<P>Now you may say "I know people who have crashed like that and didn't get hurt and they weren't wearing a seat belt" well lucky them, they can thank the automotive engineers for the safe design of padded dashes and collapsable steering wheels.<P>Any thoughts on holding babies or children in your lap as a passenger and not having them in a car seat?<P>I call that a "Baby Airbag".<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
