Z||000075||Rex||06-16-2001||11:47 AM||||I have read some very nice real life stories in this thread about wearing seatbelts, hats off to you all. Why would somone not want to wear a seatbelt? hmmmmmmm  never in a serious accident. never saw a serious accident. thinks it wont happen to me.too lazy.just undereducated in general.Buckle up man!!, its OK you wont look like a wimp.A state tropper said" I've never unbuckled a dead man"  or woman.   Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000076||Galen||06-16-2001||11:54 AM||||hey hoho, if 30mph is 30feet, would 55 be 55ft? if so, I feel I could fall from 55ft and not get hurt, I slammed that solid metal no padding 76 ford f100 dash at 55 with no belt  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> lucky me? who knows.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/redcreature.gif">     <BR> <A HREF="mailto:galen@spinrpg.com">galen@spinrpg.com</A>  -<A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe w/ sunroof</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Pictures</A>||||reg||1
Z||000077||84Bill||06-16-2001||12:42 PM||||Yeah ok ok Personal choice, Law , common sense, pro choice, anti abortion, ect. ect.<BR>What does this thread boil down to?<BR> <BR>From what I see here one side feels the other side should do what they are told by the other side. What I honestly feel here is that everyone here has a mind and everyone here can use that mind to choose for themselves what is right and wrong for their needs and the "laws" should reflect that need accordingly. Instead of imposing on individual desires. If you don't want a seatbelt fine then statisticly speaking you will be hurt worse should an accident occour then your preimum should reflect your need for that freedom. A Please sign here clause on an insurance card stating you don't wear a seatbelt and your premium doubles. If you don't sign and get caught without one on then your premium triples. If unsigned and you get in an accident and get hurt your premium quadruples. Thats a smart law. and wearing a seatbelt is a smart thing to do.<P>I have been educated in the school of hard knocks and I can tell you that I wear a seatbelt as a result of it. Not because it's the law. <BR>On the other side of the coin, I have smoke detectors and fire extinguishers in my home and garage as well as a CO2 detector, Why? Because statistics have shown that my family and I have a better chance of survival with that equipment in place. I have not had the unfortunate first hand expierence to show the need for it but I have seen and heard what can happen if I don't have it. <BR>It's my choice and increasing my famlies chances of surviving a fire in my home. <BR>There is no law requireing me to have it and for those of you that don't have this equipment in your home, well good luck to you. I don't feel sorry for people that burn up and kill themselves because they were just not smart enough to realize the benefits of life and property preserving equipment.<P>I also carry fire extinquishers in all my cars. Why? because I don't want to have to sit back like and idiot and watch my car burn to the ground because I didn't have an 8 dollar piece of equipment. Yes the total cost of this was extriemly high at a grand total of 25 bucks or so. My seat belt is free by comparison.<BR>Again I know what can happen if I don't have it. I have never had a car fire to show me first hand that I need it and I really don't need first hand expierence. <BR>My insurance company doesn't give me a break because I carry one, I wish they would but then again they are money grubbing legal shammers. I have no real incentives to carry an extinguisher others than the chances a fire will cause less damage to my car if I do have it available.<P>So if we set aside the law and look at what we have here. It would appear that we have a lot of potential Darwin award winners and every nite at 6:00 I see a parade of them on the evening news and think to myself. humm I wonder what I can do to prevent that from happening to me or my family.<P>So in closeing it can be said that With knowledge is power. Knowledge is ones capacity to know. Power is the ability to do something.<BR>So inversly put, Dumbness is weak. <BR>Dont go confusing the statement by saying I can bench press 500 pounds ther for I can beat you up and that makes me powerfull. what I'm saying is that you are dumb aka weak minded and powerless to save yourself in an event of and accident or emergency.<BR>Yes I do agree that the law about seatbelts is dumb<P>Nuff said<BR>Thanks for reading||||reg||14
Z||000078||JSocha||06-16-2001||03:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84Bill:<BR><B>So if we set aside the law and look at what we have here. It would appear that we have a lot of <I>potential Darwin award winners</I> and every nite at 6:00 I see a parade of them on the evening news and think to myself. humm I wonder what I can do to prevent that from happening to me or my family.<P>So in closeing it can be said that With knowledge is power. Knowledge is ones capacity to know. Power is the ability to do something.<BR>So inversly put, <I>Dumbness</I> is weak. <BR>Dont go confusing the statement by saying I can bench press 500 pounds ther for I can beat you up and that makes me powerfull. what <I>I'm saying is that you are dumb aka weak minded and powerless to save yourself</I> in an event of and accident or emergency.<BR>Yes I do agree that the law about seatbelts is dumb</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I was going to stay out of this by sitting on my hands and just read instead of responding, however, once again I need to point out the fact how "name calling" and/or "classifying" an individual because of their belief, opinion or just they don't fit within the normal paradigm of most individuals on this forum and must resort to this, just shows me how low some people are willing to go.<P>And yes, I will personally admit, I am, can be and have been just as guilty.  Now we <B>all</B> need to crawl out, not from the bottom of the barrell, but from underneath it.<P>As I feel, not to mention many others, that this is totally uncalled for.<P>I have no problems with wearing a seatbelt.  Wouldn't bother me in the least.  Yet I choose not to.  If I die, who is to say I would not have died with it on. We do not have the ability to back up the "time line" to see if it would have or would not have made a difference.  "I wonder Jeff, what would have happened now if the exact same conditions to which you wore you seatbelt can be reproduced with one minor change, that this time the seat belt is not there". yada-yada-yada...  We do not have that ability.<P>So you could say that "research has proved" (which in the relm of science, nothing is proven, it is only shown until something else overrides the findings and ie would disprove the current theory), yet it is all "speculative" and "what if".  No two incidents are identical.<P>We all have space!  Why?  So we don't do it in the same place twice and so that nothing occurs exactly in the same place twice.<P>The relavent point is still "choice".  You, I, my next door neighbor, etc. have this right.  And you know full well how certain people abuse it by trying to tell you what to do...where you I can guarantee will tell the individual stepping on your toes..."mind your own business!".  Well then, how do you know that your business wasn't actually conflicting with their business?<P>For example, and I laugh to this day about it because of the hilarity of the situation.<P>Our new house has a telescopicing 20' flag pole outside on our deck.<P>We don't have an American Flag however, I do have a big red flag with a broad white diagnal stripe from the upper corner of one end to the lower end of the other.<P>So, and in order to test the stress of this telescoping pole (as no flag has ever been put on it), I put it up.<P>Immidate reaction from the golfers at the golf course we are next to and as well the people in our community is "You can't be flying that flag;  Take it down;  You have no right to fly another countries flag; Are you a communits;  Why are you supporting another country since your an American; An American flag is to go on your pole and nothing else!; blah-blah-blah;"<P>I finally did take it down, after I, my wife and my step daughters had the best laugh in our entire lives, not because "they" wanted me to, but recently because of the weather.<P>BTW, the flag was a SCUBA diving flag and I do support the preservation of under water life and the coral reefs!  Not because I have to, but because I choose to.<P>Pierce county was complaining about the mosquito population and that every one in town should do their part in controlling them by keeping their grass cut, items that could trap water, poison on the ground, etc.<P>Well, I'm doing my part especially during this wet weather we are experiencing, so out of eight electric bug zappers, I have one 20' up in the air on and at the top of the flag pole.<P>Guess what?  Everybody is complaining about that now and that I don't have the right.   Its my frickin flag pole!<P>Or our house, especially in the small community of Rugby where the guy who built it, basically built a monument to himself and we just happen to have the luxury of buying it from his since he is being moved to Florida.<P>People feel we have "no right" to live in this house and that this house is not to be lived in, but "toured".<P>So therefore, as you can imagine, I am sick and tired of people who feel that what I choose to do, what I have the priveledge or luxury to do, etc., feels that they can tell me what I need to do and call me every name under the sun, because I do not personally agree with them or fit in their paradigm.<P>Regarding laws.  Yes, certain laws are there to protect us, make our lives better, etc., as a society in whole.<P>However, they can go overboard with them as well.  I'm also old enough to know as well as decide for myself that I don't need someone there telling me which way to wipe my @$$!<P>I don't know who KW works for as an Engineer, if it is a manufacturer, however, our company is a member of NAM (National Association of Manufacturers).<P>If you knew how many laws goverenment, goverenment organizations and lobby groups that goverenment officials are trying to pass daily without your knowledge and that are so damn ludacrist to begin with, you would be absolutely amazed and would be taking action, like many business people do, against making sure many of these "under the table" laws that are in the senate or whatever do not affect many of you and/or see the light of day.<P>Ever wonder why poloticians are so damn eager to get reelected?<P>Because they would not make it in the world that we have to and are forced to live in daily with all the dumb laws they have passed just so they can keep there cushy little high paying jobs!  That's why!<P>You don't believe me, take a moment to visit <A HREF="http://www.amerikanexpose.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.amerikanexpose.com</A>   (there's another website as well) They are constantly uncovering laws that are being secretly worked on that effect you and I.  Alot of them negative!<P>At that site, take time to find out more about the real NAFTA Corridor!  We see fictional movies about big cities where people are hearded into them so that "big brother" can control, monitor and regulate the people.  Many of us see it as science fiction...and yet its starting to happen!  Look at older movies and compare them to what is happening today where we probably all said, "Man!  I'm glad that will never happen here in America".<P>When will the goverenment decide to draw the line if we always allow them to take our choices away, such as this ridiculous seat belt issue?<P>One day we could end up like the people of China with their family planning program, where your only allowed one child and if your attempt fails, tough.  You are only allowed one opportunity.  Well, there goes our rights for us to reproduce so that our specific prodginy or heritage line can carry on.<P>How about other countries under Martial Law.  Lets say here, goverenmently regulated that we as individuals are to be locked in our houses and off the streets by 6PM to 6AM, for example.  No exceptions otherwise thrown in jail, or worse yet shot because somebody else views you as a criminal to which the law was enacted to protect society.<P>On a closing note, anyone been to the White House in Washington DC?  What is the first thing they tell you on the tour?<P>You are to refer to the President as "Mr. President" and nothing else.  You are not permitted to call them by their first and/or their last name, otherwise they will escort you out.<P>I thought that is why America fought Britian!  To get away from Britians laws, have the right to all freedoms including that of choice and to get away from the tyranny and the labels to which the commoners were forced to abide by because somebody was higher on the social latter then themselves and to do so they could be punished for their actions.<P>Well everyone, wake up...because we are all allowing it to happen again and nobody is saying "hey, we need to draw the line on certain issues here".<P>Should we debate "Gun Control" now?  How about the right and choice for you to hunt?  Your right to smoke in public?<P>Yes "knowledge is power".  It seems Uncle Sam is a lot smarter then most of us though and has the financial backing to support it to which you and I do pay dearly for whether it is right and/or is wrong.<P>And inversly, "Ignorance is Bliss".  And there is a lot of happy people out here.<P>84Bill, name call away, classify me the way you want, that is your choice and I can do nothing about it.  I ask that you just rememeber, a sword can cut both ways.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||13
Z||000079||Songman||06-16-2001||04:39 PM||||I tried to warn you! heheh They will never see that it is choice. These are the same people that think that only the people in their church will be in Heaven... These so-called intelligent people that have to resort to name calling...<P>As I said before, I will compare IQ's with anyone here to see if there is a lack of intelligence on my part. Some may think that because I am an entertainer and have long hair and ride a Harley that I'm not all that smart. Well, luckily I was just able to get out of that corporate rut that I was in for all of those years because I had a talent that would make my life easier. As for IQ, some questioned it after my comment. I won't say specifically, but I could be in MENSA with my scores on the test... I just choose not to be a Lemming and feel like I have to follow the crowd. <P>What do you know? A whole post without even mentioning a seatbelt! Oops... I just mentioned it... heheh<P>As JSocha said, we are not taking this as personally as those on the other side of the fence. I consider you all friends, even though most of you have attacked my intelligence in this thread. You just keep on living like you choose to live and I will do the same. And I promise to try not to cost you too much while I am doing it...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000080||84Bill||06-16-2001||04:46 PM||||I got an Idea<BR>We take 2 identical cars run them up to 40 mph and into a wall. I wear belts and you don't and then, when were done we can compare notes. That is if you and I survive. I can safely say I have a much better chance of surviving and avoiding serious injury than you do, HANDS DOWN Then we'll roll the same cars down a hill again me belted you not (provided you have enough recovery time and guts left from the above test) Oh and trust me I'll do this test if you will. I have done many stupid things in my time and I will be happy to add this to my long list.<BR>Hey wait, I called myself stupid. huh, go figure. I'll guess that means your smart not to take up the challange.<BR>As far as laws are concerned yeah some are stupid and dumb and outrageous. <BR>2000 people a <B>day</B>die in automobile accidents and a <B>fraction</B> of that number die every day from hand gun related incidents. Yet we have the most ridgid laws controlling guns than we do cars. <BR>Hell I can't get a gun myself yet I can <B>drive</B> an even more deadlier weapon than a gun.<BR>I have no criminal record, no records that I can find anywhere to prevent me from buying a gun yet every time I go for a background check I get turned down and the worst part is they won't tell me why I failed! Laws are whacked I agree with you there. but laws are what we all must live and die by.<P>And Sccha my friend I would not like to live next to you with that flag pole you got there and see all that stuff flailing in the air BUT then again in the event of a storm it's reassuring to know that I have a lightning rod right next door to me that will protect my home in the event of a lightning strike    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>Peace<BR>Thanks songman I hope we never have to pay a dime extra on you than we have too   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-16-2001).]||||reg||1
