Z||000087||JSocha||06-16-2001||06:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>I tried to warn you! heheh</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah my friend, I know.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Just the "p*ss, vinger and apparently all that sugar" coursin through my body that has me riled up for a good argument and debate.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>84Bill, as I said, we can not turn back the "time line" of an incident.  <P>Your logic, go head to head and see who fares better or worse.  <P>My logic, compare a particular incident with the same individual, but there is no magic wand that can do it or button in life for "REPLAY".  Big, big difference.<P>On another note, and I'm not targeting this at any particular individual so the you and your is very, very open:<P>Did I say your way was right?  No<BR>Did I say your way was wrong?  No<P>Did I say my way was right? No<BR>Did I say my way was wrong? No<P>Very "neutral"<P>This is open to interpretation, but this is how it is going so far as I or any others might be perceiving it:<P>Did you say your way was right? ie, Yes<BR>Did you say your way was wrong? No<P>Did you say my way was right? No<BR>Did you say my was was wrong? ie, Yes<P>Does this seem to be very neutral to anyone?  Not in my opinion.<P>Once again, the question of this topic was "who wears their seatbelts?".  <P>Many of you said "I do", however, the very moment one said "I don't" and at the same time did not put the ones that said "I do" down, you jumped his ship, swords drawn ready to draw blood, that including Galen, Songman and myself.<P>Three pages later, here we all are, either name calling, classifing, belittling or whatever else, while I have tried, to the best of my abilities in my posts not to stoop to this level, keep it more that this is my "choice" and at the same time respect your choice to wear them, as stated above in my questions to try and point out neutrality.<P>It went from whats your choice, to social political, to bashing fellow forum members who have elected, and in most cases probably against the law within their respective states based on their legislative rules, to not wear them.  And in most cases, like me, if caught, I pay the respective 20-25 dollar fine imposed in our state.<P>You want to preach about that we should follow the laws set down, such as wearing a seatbelt.  <P>Okay, well, as most bibles or religions preache (5 years of Catholic School, ugly nuns and strict priest, even though I don't believe as previously stated), "Let he who is without sin cast the first stone."<P>How many laws have you broken in your lifetime because you felt they were not for you?  How about today...how many laws?  Speeding?  Rolling through a stop sign?  Pedistrian right of way?  Insurance fraud to get a better adjustment? etc....<P>If you say, well, I don't break any...then I just have to say I feel sorry for you that are in denial.  Everyone breaks some law in some way.<P>Any people of Oklahoma I call upon you now, and I can't remember if this was a common law or if it is actually still a law enforced today...<P>How's your s*x life?  <BR>How about the pleasures you are allowed to practice?  <BR>How about 0r@l, giving/receiving?  <P>Care to eloborate now for those not aware of the law I am now talking about?  <P>How many of you break the specific law  imposed (& yes, you can plead the 5th if you wish) to enjoy a pleasure that fullfills you?  Do you feel this should be your choice no matter what anybody says?<P>How many of you enjoy s#x? (rhetorical question!)<P>How many of you would immidately be breaking the law regarding s#x if one was imposed upon you today by our goverenment to a specific act or acts, but damn it, you enjoy it and feel it is your choice and would not want retaliation when someone asks your opinion on the topic?<P>The defense, as it has now become for me, now rests!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||5
