Z||000095||Voytek2||06-17-2001||09:04 PM||||JSocha and Songman: I have respect for all people on this forum (well.... most, anyways) , includging you guys.  You've had some pretty good posts over the period of time I've been here.  You make some good points on the seatbelt thing, too.  Just for the record: I didn't call anyone here stupid. I said that we have elected officials because some people are too stupid to think for themselves.  No one in particular.  That being said, I think I'll leave this post.  Ok, I'll leave in as soon as I summarize some things  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> : JSocha: the gov't IS interfering with our lives too much - there's no question about it.  The seatbelt laws don't fall into that category.  Your hypothesis about turning back the time does not make sense.  84Bill said 'let's run our cars into a wall at a certain speed, I will wear a seatbelt and you won't'.  I don't think you'd need to turn back the time on that one.  The answer is simple and straight forward w/o ANALizing this to death.  Besides, this HAS been re-done time and time again with dummies (no name calling intended).  The conclusions, made by some very competent people, are always the same.  Case closed.<BR>Songman: Having great knowledge and a high IQ does not always mean that one possesses a great deal of common sense.  In fact, bringing up your IQ several times in this thread when no one has directly questioned it, can be dangerous to the health of your IQ.  There is more testimony FOR seatbelts in this thread than against, regardless of what the law says.  Draw your own conclusions gentlemen.<BR>P.S.<BR>I will STILL speed occasionally, even though I know it is illegal, I know it is dangerous and I know it can cost me money (or health). If you start a thread on the forum telling me the dangers associated with speeding, I will be there to support you.||||reg||1
Z||000096||Songman||06-17-2001||09:16 PM||||I understand your point, although my IQ (intelligence quotient) was questioned on several occasions in this thread, not necessarily by you...<P>Also, this thread does lean more towards people thinking the gov't does not interfere by trying to make us wear seat belts. I think that is why JSocha listed the other thread where it went the other way.<P>Bottomw line... you're never gonna get a good idea of where the forum as a whole stands because most people have learned that it does no good to throw yourself in front of angry mob as JSocha and I have done. But I believe that standing up for what you believe in is part of being a man. At least that is what my grandfather taught me. But then of course, he came from a time when cars had metal dashboards and no seatbelts too, and the government pretty much let people decide for themselves what was in their best interest as long as they weren't harming anyone....<P>Ahhh... the good ole days. I have long said that I was born too late...<P>Everybody have a good night... and let's please let this thread die in peace. I thought we had done that since me and Bill made our little jokes...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
