Z||000114||JSocha||06-18-2001||03:14 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>so <P> 30 mph is like falling 3 stories<BR> 55 mph is like falling 10 stories<BR> 70 mph is like falling 16 stories<P>  I dont think any of these are considered surviable without a seat belt. If you want to try it, cut the dash board and windsheild out of the car of your choice, lay it on the sidewalk with the part you would hit in a wreck facing up, then leap from the window of your choice into the dashboard/windsheild.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.synergizedsolutions.com/simpsons/pictures/homer/homerpoint.gif">  <B>So, if I understand this right, in order to survive, I would be wiser to buckle up and jump out of a window with just a car seat strapped to my butt?</B><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.synergizedsolutions.com/simpsons/pictures/homer/homer_snacks.gif">  <B>Well, I better get some goodies for this show! Who's going to start?  hehehehe</B><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 06-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000115||84Bill||06-18-2001||03:19 PM||||Duh!||||reg||1
Z||000116||Ken Wittlief||06-18-2001||03:47 PM||||To test it at 30 mph buckle into a car pointing downwards, and then get dropped car and all 3 stories.<P> (a 3 story fall BTW means you jump out the 4th floor window, not the 3rd).<P>  when the car hits it will start to crumple and transfer the deceleration to the seat, which transfers it to you, so you decelerate over a distance of 2 feet.<P>  if youre not wearing your seatbelt then the car comes to a complete stop before you hit the dash, so the car is going zero when you hit the dash, and you are still going 30. Since this happens in 1/10th of a second, you will not have a chance to brace yourself or hang on.<P>  so when you are not wearing your belt, its like falling 3 stories into the dashboard of a car that is not moving. Then you go from 30 to 0 in a distace of about 2 inches (the thickness of the padding on the dash, and how far your face gives) instead of a distance of 2 feet.||||reg||1
Z||000117||Galen||06-18-2001||03:53 PM||||basicly it hurts, but that hurt should be a personal choice, not something the goverment says you can't feel. Besides, children are hell, but the goverment lets ya have them. beer can kill, but you can drink it..<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/angryboy.gif">      <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:galen@spinrpg.com">galen@spinrpg.com</A>   -<A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe w/ sunroof</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Pictures</A>||||reg||1
Z||000118||Ken Wittlief||06-18-2001||03:58 PM||||This is also the reason why seatbelts are designed to prevent injuries in the fore and aft direction. when you are driving all your velocity is forward. unless you skid the car sideways, when you hit you will hit forward.<P> If you hit a solid object you will loose all your forward velocity in the impact, ie 30mph =&gt; 30 to 0.<P> but if you are broadsided, then your velocity after the impact is a sum of momentum equation between your cars mass and the mass and speed of the car that hit you. So if you are in a fiero, and a fiero Tbones you at 30mph, you will end up going sideways with a velocity change of 0 to 15mph after the impact.<P>   Half the speed, then your tires will skid you to a stop. For a car to sustain side impacts as well as front one, it would need to have 4 to 5 feet of crunch-zone on both sides, like it does front and rear, and our cars would look like flying saucers.<P>  so leaping to the other side of the car (I wanna see that in a fiero by the way) when you see a T bone coming still wont save you, cause 1/10th of a second the left side of the car is still gonna come over and smack you. You cant hang on at 180 Gs.<P>   The better plan is to steer or brake out of the T bone, but if you could avoid it in the first place...<P>let me re-phrase that, if you have time enough to see a T bone coming, and think, I better jump over to the other side of the car, and then actually jump, then most likely you could have breked or steered out of the whole accident instead.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000119||JSocha||06-18-2001||04:14 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>1) (a 3 story fall BTW means you jump out the 4th floor window, not the 3rd).<P>2) You cant hang on at 180 Gs.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>1a) Unless of course you are on the 14th floor which in actuality is the 13th for those who are supersticious!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>2a)  At 180 G's I think my blood would be lead at that point, my drawers would be full and I would be dead irregardless from the G force and the wearing or not wearing of seatbelts!  The "force" won't be with me that day!<P>That will conclude our mathmatical and physics class lesson for today and remember your assignments are due Wednesday and the test is still this Friday and is still based on 100 points...each question worth 10 points.  Bring your sliderules!<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Glad I could help out!<P><BR>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 06-18-2001).]||||reg||10
