Z||000128||fyerstarter||06-19-2001||08:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>basicly it hurts, but that hurt should be a personal choice, not something the goverment says you can't feel. Besides, children are hell, but the goverment lets ya have them. beer can kill, but you can drink it..<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>On the other hand Marijuana does not kill. The government knows this. Why do you think there is such a thing as prescription marijuna?It wouldn't make much sense to take a drug to cure illness if it is going to kill you would there?. Anyone want to take a guess why it's illegal? It's not too hard if you just follow the money trail.<P>Because anyone can grow it. The government cannot make any money off of it, they can't tax it, sell it, or regulate it in any way. The only thing they can do is make it illegal. <P>Our government has transformed from an elected body working in the best interest of the people to a business. And just like every modern business they have a gimmick. That gimmick is freedom and safety and serving the public interest. But like most businesses it is only used as a front to make $$<P>Do you really believe your insurance company when they say in their commercials "We care about protecting you and your family, that is why we bla bla bla....."?<P>Well the government is selling you the same bullshit. And the American public is eating it up. Everyone is always willing to trade away a little bit of their personal freedom in exchange for some peace of mind.<P>Here's an equation for you:<P>Risk=Freedom<P>therefore if risk =0 , then freedom = 0<P>If everyone were strapped to a hospital bed in a rubber room 24 hours a day, fed intravenously, and monitored constantly by a team of medical professionals then there would be minimal risk to your health. But only at the sacrifice of personal freedom. The moment you step outside you run the risk of getting hit by a truck, or catching a disease, or falling down some stairs.<P>We are all going to die sometime. There is no sense living your life in constant fear of death or injury. Life is only as valuable as it's contents. If you stay strapped to that bed your entire life maybe you will live 130 years! Or maybe you can live your life how you want to for a mere 20 years.<P>I know which I would choose.<BR>||||reg||1
