Z||000130||fierohoho||06-19-2001||09:01 AM||||You know that seatbelts are a one time use deal right? <P>They stretch in a good impact and if the car is fixed they must then be replaced. <P>What if the previous owner replaced your seatbelt with one from a junk yard wreck because he spilled his shake on it and you don't know it's used. <P>Not to make you paranoid.<P><BR>..who's that behind you...<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000131||Ken Wittlief||06-19-2001||09:53 AM||||Two cars hitting square head on with each car going 55mph is the same as one car hitting a concrete wall at 55mph, if both cars weigh the same.<P>  the instant after impact both cars will have stopped dead.<P>  A car going 55 hitting a parked car, or a car at a red lite, is like hitting a concrete wall at 27.5 mph. the instant after the impact both cars will be moving at 27.5mph, so the change in speed for the moving car is 27.5mph<P>  the reason SUVs are claimed to be safer is becase if your 2,000 lb car hits a 6,000 lb SUV headon, both going 55mph, after the impact the SUV will still be going forwards at 39mph, and you will be going backwards at 39mph.<P>  so for the people in the SUV, they went from 55 to 39, so its like hitting a wall at 16mph<P>  you went from +55 to -39mph so its like you hit a wall at 94mph.<P>  so the way they gain safety for themselves is by insuring the death of the passengers in smaller cars they hit.||||reg||1
