Z||000134||84Bill||06-19-2001||12:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by drednot:<BR><B>Wow!!  This is some string I started.  I still won't wear mine.  never had any problems with the cops.  my trick is, don't run the hell in to things, and you won't need them.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So lets see. You must drive the Mach5 and your name is really Speed right? Because when an old geezer blows the stop and in the 3.5 seconds you have to react, you press the jump button and leap unharmed over the offending car.<BR>Cool, hook me up with Pops for that modification will you? in the meantime I'll just use my seatbelt  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>Oh and please keep Spridle and ChimpChimp out of the trunk and properly belted in the back seat, it's just not safe back there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||6
Z||000135||Ken Wittlief||06-19-2001||12:15 PM||||Lets see, how many kinds of accidents are there:<P>  the ones that you plan on having<P>  the ones where you do something stupid and cause a wreck<P>  the ones where something breaks on your car and you lose control of it.<P>  the ones where someone else decides to kill themself and take someone with them (happened a couple years ago, 5 minutes before I pulled out onto the same road)<P>  the ones where someone else does something stupid and crashes into you, or pulls out in front of you<P>  the ones where someone else does poor maintance work, and something breaks on their car, and they end up hitting you<P> the ones where something falls off a truck into your path<P>  the storm accidents, where a tree limb or phone poll falls into the road where you dont expect it to be, or worst yet, falls onto your car, or falling rocks<P>   large animal ends up under your front end and you cant steer, or large bird shatters your windsheld and you can see<P>  unexpected fog, ice on bridge, whiteout, chain reaction collisions, hydroplaning<P>  drunken driver in another vehicle<P>  which ones of these do you think you have control over?!<P>  oops, i forgot a big one - other driver has medical problem (heart attack...) car is on autopilot going 70mph. Some guy with no license who was repeatedly told by his doc "DO NOT DRIVE" had an eptelectic sezure while driving a caddy here last year and ran down a cop (pedistrian on his beat). It happens.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-19-2001).]||||reg||1
