Z||000138||84Bill||06-19-2001||12:36 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>   1a) Unless of course you are on the 14th floor which in actuality is the 13th for those who are supersticious!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>2a)  At 180 G's I think my blood would be lead at that point, my drawers would be full and I would be dead irregardless from the G force and the wearing or not wearing of seatbelts!  The "force" won't be with me that day!<P>That will conclude our mathmatical and physics class lesson for today and remember your assignments are due Wednesday and the test is still this Friday and is still based on 100 points...each question worth 10 points.  Bring your sliderules!<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Glad I could help out!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry but I missed this blerb<BR>The body can sustain very high G's for a very brief moment. The government has put extensive research into this since fighter pilots can experience short high G loads better than they can sustaine long realitivly low G loads. I don't remember what the exact numbers were but I do recall over 100 G's in a few millisecond impulse is tolerable. It will surly knock the krap out of you as well as whatever you may be holding.<P>FYI There is a record holder for this. A guy went from several hundred mph to 0 over a very short distance. he was bleeding from his eyes, nose and ears and promiced never to do that again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I think he also did the first tests of ejection seats for fighter aircraft and he is still alive to this day.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-19-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000139||JSocha||06-19-2001||12:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>which ones of these do you think you have control over?!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Whether or not I maintain the personal choice  to use my seatbelt, irregardless who thinks they can tell me otherwise!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Everyone, you can not change someone else.  You can only change yourself to adapt to the circumstances at hand.<P>Whether it was said by Dale Carnagie, The Prentice Hall Group, etc., someone in there should have stated that already.<P>Ooooops!  I forgot...I recently died when I jumped out the 17th floor window with nothing but a car seat strapped to my butt using a seatbelt.<P>It must be that the "Laws of Cartoons" are more governing and allow us to do this!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.synergizedsolutions.com/simpsons/pictures/bart/bartsilly.gif"> <BR>Hey everybody!  I'm Back!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.synergizedsolutions.com/simpsons/pictures/bart/bartdance3.gif"> <BR>&lt;singing&gt;<BR>Do a little dance,<BR>Make a little love,<BR>Get down tonight!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
