Z||000146||Songman||06-19-2001||04:20 PM||||I got one for you, since we are talking songs now.... and from my favorite country singer and mentor, Merle Haggard...<P>Mama's Prayers <BR>Written by Merle Haggard<P>One night while we were driving across the mighty Texas plains<BR>A car pulled out with it's headlights out headlong into our lane<BR>As Deanrow swerved to miss the car, I felt a mighty hand<BR>Somehow my mama's prayers had worked again...<BR>--<P>And I didn't even have to change the words. I didn't see one mention of seatbelts at all.<P>I said way back when this thread started that we can all post instances to back our position on whether or not seatbelts are good or not. And this is true. But that is not the issue. The issue is STILL whether or not you have a choice in something that involves your safety. And the answer is STILL, yes you should.<P>I have STILL yet to call anyone a name. I have STILL yet to attack anyone personally. And I STILL don't wear my seatbelt. And I STILL will go to Bill's house for dinner next time I am in PA.<P>And you know the main thing -- I don't really care. I am more worried about getting the FieroLisa thread in O/T over the 400 posts mark and it is even more ridiculous than this thread... But at least it is fun! hehe<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||12
