Z||000148||JSocha||06-19-2001||04:27 PM||||Say Ken, is there a direct and relational purpose to the songs you wish to sing against Songman?<P>I don't wear my seat belt either, electively I might add, if you have not noticed?<P>And to resolve whether or not I shoudl wear it, I have decided to ride my bicycle and/or let my wife drive, as she wears hers all the time (even after the accidents):<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.umr.edu/~cycle/calhobbes/calhobs_.gif"> <P>And for those of you who are on this Traffic Safety Campaign, this is all I have to say to that matter!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.umr.edu/~cycle/calhobbes/slogan.gif"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000149||Ken Wittlief||06-19-2001||04:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>   ...I bet you voted for Gore, didn't you? ...Thank God we got rid of him.. I hope that island ...is big enough for all of <P>you people...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> sorry - gotta call you on this one.<P>  making assumptions on someones political position - lumping someone in with Gore and Baldwin<P>  and referring to any person or group of people as 'you people'<P> is personal<P>and it is name calling.<P> if you label someone with one word, or refer to the person with the three sentance long definition of the word, you are still naming them.<P>  remember back when Ross Perot was addressing an audiance of black americans, and referred to them as 'you people' - even though what he said was a positive remark he still caught bloody h3ll for saying it.<P>   so I find it humorous that you repeatedly make personal statements about others in this thread, and assign or assume qualities to their character<P>  but then say, 'at least I havent resorted to name calling'.<P>||||reg||1
