Z||000151||Songman||06-19-2001||05:27 PM||||I think I will have to refer to you a book called "I Haven't Understood Anything Since 1962" by Lewis Grizzard, a great American.<P>He dedicates a whole chapter to the Speech Police. As a matter of fact, it is the first chapter. I could copy the entire 30 pages since it is so relavent here, but I won't since poor Mr Grizzard is dead and I wouldn't want him to be attacked and not be here to defend himself.<P>Basically, the Speech Police is any person or group of people who search word for word for anything people say or write, to see if they can find some inferred item to take exception to. This is done to try to make the other person's side of an argument lose credibilty, when it fact has nothing to do with the argument at all.<P>To take a quote from this book... "That's what the Speech Police have done. They have made the American Tradition of speaking one's mind almost a hanging offense. But what if one speaks his mind and it is the truth? THE TRUTH? What's the truth got to do with anything?... How the Speech Police have managed to deal with THE TRUTH is they started something called <I>Political Correctness</I>, which is fairly easy to define. It means <I>keep your mouth shut, even if it is true because we don't care about truth anymore.</I><P>Now to respond to your personal things against me... Yes, I did say YOU PEOPLE. YOU PEOPLE in this thread who are so dead set for making us all do things YOUR way.<P>Yes, I did make assumptions about your political beliefs based on what you have shown in this thread, that being a total lack of respect for the Constitution of this United States, which tells us that the gov't has it's job but controlling it's citizens is not listed in that job description. Al Gore also shows this, and Alec Baldwin made his statements very public as you have.<P>Have I questioned your intelligence or that of any other here? Have I called you any sort of derogatory name? Have I tried in any way to say that you are not entitled to your opinion? Have I made up stupid ass little songs replacing the words so as to make a direct assault at you? Have I been the one posting every other message trying to come up with some scientific theory that makes me right and the rest of the world wrong? The answer is HELL NO! Because even though I disagree with you on seatbelts AND what it takes to respect another human being, I have tried to stay focused on one point. I have even tried to stay out of this when I saw how far you intended to go with it. Everyone else here is willing to get along regardless of which side of the fence they are on, but for some reason you chose me to carry on with.<P>I'm just a good ole Southern boy, but I was raised to respect people. No one has ever accused me of treating anyone unfairly and they will never have a reason to do so. You think I am costing you? Well, I think you are costing me. This country is going to hell because of the Speech Police where everyone gets dragged across the coals anytime someome finds a forum where they can get an audience and a little backing. As I said earlier, in this thread you are right, there are more PRO-seatbelt people talking. But that is only in this thread. There have been plenty of others where it went the other way. Personally, I don't give a damn what you think of me, but if you want to make this a personal thing with me, I am more than open to the challenge.<P>I'll say one more thing... Do I have an opinion in my head about you? Has it changed since the beginning of this thread? The answer to both is yes. But I will keep that to myself. The only thing I am going to say publicly is try giving the same respect that you seem to want from people when you post this stuff...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||8
