Z||000158||Ken Wittlief||06-20-2001||09:24 AM||||geeze - do I have to put the little smiley face on every line that is intended to be humorous or tongue in cheek to keep people from getting upset?!<P>  the song paraphrases are my feeble attempt at humor to lighten up the discussion.<P> so was my whole last post - you put up posts that commit the logical fallicy of discussing ANYTHING about the other people, then you have made a personal comment about the other person - its called ad hominum or something like that.<P> I said there is nothing in the consitiution about wearing seatbelts, or about motor vehicles - you come back, and instead of discussing the relationship between the constitution and motor vehicle regulations, you come back and say - "you must have voted for Gore..."<P>  who I voted for, or who is elegible to be in Mensa, or whos 'intelligence needs to be questioned' or who is from the south - has nothing to do with what happens to someone when they are not wearing a seatbelt.<P>  it also has nothing to do with whether we should be free to choose how we will drive our cars on a public transportation system, and whether we have a RIGHT to drive, or whether it is a privalidge granted by the government. <P> (BTW it is a privalidge, not a right. If you dont think so, get stopped without a license and tell the judge "I got rights!" see how far that goes)<P>   If someone asserts the constitiution has nothing to say about vehicle safety, how does anyone conclude that person does not believe in the constitiution?!<P>   IT WAS SUPPOSE TO BE FUNNY - doesnt anyone else see the humor in this - you make all kinds of personal unrelated remakes, and then say 'at least I didnt get personal...'<P> It IS funny! Im only pointing it out. Nothing on this forum is intended to be a personal attack against anyone BUT i can disagree with your stance on an issue. Since your stance is your personal take, and my position is my personal opinion, how can it not be personal???<P>  Isnt that what a FORUM is?! You stand up and say what you think, then someone else stands up and says what they think? If one is not allowed to refer to the other persons statements, or to the other person, then there wont be much of a discussion going on. And if we all keep our opinions to ourselves then this would be a pretty empty website.<P>  one last thing on this fasination with namecalling. Certain statements are commonly used to establish a reference point, such as, "Are you NUTS!!!" Its a short and concise way to establish the level of disagreement, the one extreem or the other. Its not intended to question you mental stability, neither are comments like 'you boneheads' or 'not wearing a seatbelt is stupid'.<P>  Even the most intelligent people do stupid things sometimes.<P> For example: Im starting to think it was stupid for me to express any of my personal views on this forum, since I mostly seem to be pissing people off.||||reg||1
Z||000159||elfiero||06-20-2001||09:55 AM||||Ken,you were talking about pulling "g's"-did<BR>you know that indy cars have g-meters on <BR>them?.A couple years ago little al unser ran<BR>into a wall and the "black box" said he pulled 79G's!.Now for the interesting part,<BR>those of you who follow CART will know what<BR>I mean-ever scince,when he talks he just don't look or sound the same!he has kind of<BR>a glazed look and he talks a little slower<BR>than he used to.This is sad,but shows what<BR>happens when your brain hits the inside of<BR>your skull.||||reg||9
